      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right that genetics are powerful, and it makes sense to feel like you are fighting force of nature when it feels so real. However, resilience isn't about canceling out your biology, but rather building a defense system strong enough to handle specific challenges so they don't define your entire life. Imagine building a fortress that knows it has some old walls the design came with; you aren't arguing against the blueprint, you're just reinforcing the structure so your home remains safe. Many people with similar backgrounds live long, fulfilling lives exactly because they learned to build these fortresses, even when the foundation feels shaky.",
